{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PqsnjWjoaLYDKuqvx3ZyA1","type":"tool_result","content":"Wrote ../../agent/brace-inventory.json; candidate matches need manual scope review.\n## B01.1\n{\n  \"id\": \"B01.1\",\n  \"check\": \"Each agent role has one explicit allowlist of tool names, with no wildcard grants such as `*`, `mcp__*`, `Bash(*)`, or `bypassPermissions`.\",\n  \"coverage_required\": true,\n  \"verify\": \"1) Find where each agent is built and tools are passed (`allowed_tools`, `tools=[`, `allowedTools`, `.mcp.json`, `settings.json`). 2) Check each role has one fixed list of names. 3) Answer no if any list holds `*`, `mcp__*`, `Bash(*)`, a pattern or regex, `bypassPermissions`, or is built from `list_tools()`, or if a second agent role or entry point has no list.\",\n  \"candidate_sites\": []\n}\n\n## B01.2\n{\n  \"id\": \"B01.2\",\n  \"check\": \"Tools discovered from MCP servers are filtered against that allowlist before the model can see or call them.\",\n  \"coverage_required\": true,\n  \"verify\": \"1) Find MCP discovery (`list_tools`, `session.list_tools`, `tools/list`, MCP client setup). 2) Trace the result to where it is handed to the model. 3) Confirm a filter keeps only names on the allowlist. 4) Answer no if any discovered tool reaches the model unfiltered, the filter is a denylist or prefix match (`startswith`, `mcp__server__`), or a refresh or reconnect path skips it.\",\n  \"candidate_sites\": []\n}\n\n## B01.3\n{\n  \"id\": \"B01.3\",\n  \"check\": \"The dispatcher rejects a call to any tool name not on the allowlist, instead of looking it up dynamically.\",\n  \"coverage_required\": true,\n  \"verify\": \"1) Find the dispatcher (search `tool_use`, `call_tool`, `dispatch`, `execute`, `getattr`, `registry[`). 2) Check it rejects names not on the allowlist with an error. 3) Answer no if it looks tools up with `getattr`, `globals()`, `eval`, or a registry holding more than the allowlist, falls back to calling the MCP server directly, or catches the unknown-tool error and continues.\",\n  \"candidate_sites\": []\n}\n\n## B01.4\n{\n  \"id\": \"B01.4\",\n  \"check\": \"Allow and approval decisions never read server-supplied hints or descriptions such as `readOnlyHint` or 'read-only'.\",\n  \"coverage_required\": true,\n  \"verify\": \"1) Search for `readOnlyHint`, `destructiveHint`, `annotations`, `description`, and approval or auto-approve code. 2) Check whether any allow, skip-approval, or permission branch reads these. 3) Answer no if any allow or approval decision depends on a server hint or tool description text, including a default that auto-approves tools marked read-only.\",\n  \"candidate_sites\": []\n}\n\n## B01.5\n{\n  \"id\": \"B01.5\",\n  \"check\": \"File access is limited to named directories, not the whole filesystem.\",\n  \"coverage_required\": true,\n  \"verify\": \"1) Find file tools and mounts (`allowed_directories`, `cwd`, `open(`, `fs.`, `os.ReadFile`, container `volumes`, `mountPath`). 2) Check paths are resolved (`realpath`, `resolve`, `filepath.Clean`) then compared to named directories. 3) Answer no if access is unrestricted, `/` or home is mounted, the check is a string `startsWith`/prefix test without resolving `..` and symlinks, or a shell tool bypasses it.\",\n  \"candidate_sites\": []\n}\n\n## B02.2\n{\n  \"id\": \"B02.2\",\n  \"check\": \"Tenant scope is enforced in the credential or the data layer (token claim, row-level security, or per-tenant account), not by the prompt or by code the model's output controls.\",\n  \"coverage_required\": true,\n  \"verify\": \"1) Find how queries and API calls pick a tenant (search `tenant`, `org_id`, row-level security, `CREATE POLICY`, per-tenant credentials). 2) Trace where the tenant value comes from. 3) Answer no if one shared login or key reaches all tenants and the tenant ID comes from the prompt, a tool argument the model fills, or app code filtering after the query.\",\n  \"candidate_sites\": []\n}\n\n## B02.4\n{\n  \"id\": \"B02.4\",\n  \"check\": \"The acting agent is verifiably identified separately from any explicitly delegated user/system authority; it does not copy a login session or inherit a person's unrestricted permissions.\",\n  \"coverage_required\": true,\n  \"verify\": \"1) Trace each API credential to its issuer, acting identity, original subject, grants and destination. 2) Accept explicitly authorized user-delegation flows with a separately verified agent and bounded permissions. 3) Answer no for copied login sessions, personal/admin keys or inherited broad user access; a delegated OAuth access token is not by itself a failure. Answer unknown when external issuer/enforcement evidence is unavailable.\",\n  \"candidate_sites\": []\n}\n\n## B03.3\n{\n  \"id\": \"B03.3\",\n  \"check\": \"No long-lived secrets appear in prompts, Dockerfiles or image layers, or checked-in config.\",\n  \"coverage_required\": true,\n  \"verify\": \"1) Search prompt templates, Dockerfiles (`ENV`, `ARG`, `COPY .env`), `.env*`, `*.yaml`, `*.tfvars`, `.mcp.json` `env` blocks for key-like literals (`sk-`, `AKIA`, `token:`, `password:`). 2) Check prompt-building code for env values inserted into messages. 3) Answer no if any real secret is checked in, baked into an image, or placed in a prompt; `.gitignore` listing a file does not count if it is committed.\",\n  \"candidate_sites\": []\n}\n\n## B04.1\n{\n  \"id\": \"B04.1\",\n  \"check\": \"A revocation control disables the agent's own identity or credentials without disabling the user who launched it.\",\n  \"coverage_required\": true,\n  \"verify\": \"1) Find a disable or revoke path (script, runbook, IdP config, `disable`, `revoke`, deny list). 2) Check it targets the agent's own identity or credential. 3) Answer no if the agent uses the user's token, so revocation disables the user too, or no revoke path exists. Answer unknown if revocation lives only in an identity provider outside this repo.\",\n  \"candidate_sites\": []\n}\n\n## B05.2\n{\n  \"id\": \"B05.2\",\n  \"check\": \"The gate runs in the execution path when the call runs and checks the operation, the target, and the arguments, not only a tool name, command name, or blocklist of words.\",\n  \"coverage_required\": true,\n  \"verify\": \"1) Find where tool calls execute (`tool_use`, `call_tool`, `execute`, `can_use_tool`, `PreToolUse`). 2) Find the gate that runs before the side effect and see what it inspects. 3) Answer no if it checks only the tool or command name, matches words (`'rm' in cmd`, `DROP`), runs after the call, lives only in the prompt, or sits in a `try`/`catch` that continues on error. 4) For each value that lets an action skip approval (an internal recipient, a small amount, a safe path), read the comparison itself: answer no if a domain, host, or path is matched by suffix, prefix, or substring without an anchor, so `endswith('example.com')` also passes `evil-ex","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5c0e1d7c-1c3d-4042-9555-abf3c43a76e6","uuid":"a7b73110-768d-44f3-ac95-d9af56ba1198","timestamp":"2026-11-21T11:44:45.671Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"Wrote ../../agent/brace-inventory.json; candidate matches need manual scope review.\n## B01.1\n{\n  \"id\": \"B01.1\",\n  \"check\": \"Each agent role has one explicit allowlist of tool names, with no wildcard grants such as `*`, `mcp__*`, `Bash(*)`, or `bypassPermissions`.\",\n  \"coverage_required\": true,\n  \"verify\": \"1) Find where each agent is built and tools are passed (`allowed_tools`, `tools=[`, `allowedTools`, `.mcp.json`, `settings.json`). 2) Check each role has one fixed list of names. 3) Answer no if any list holds `*`, `mcp__*`, `Bash(*)`, a pattern or regex, `bypassPermissions`, or is built from `list_tools()`, or if a second agent role or entry point has no list.\",\n  \"candidate_sites\": []\n}\n\n## B01.2\n{\n  \"id\": \"B01.2\",\n  \"check\": \"Tools discovered from MCP servers are filtered against that allow