{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChG29EAENHmGDX3cJ7nJG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I reviewed B01–B05 and saved `agent/brace-findings.json`. It passes `validate_findings.py --fix --batch B01,B02,B03,B04,B05 --before-challenges` as valid: 4 gaps and 1 needs_evidence. Pre-scan had 0 hits, so there was nothing to resolve. No item is likely_pass. I did not run challenges, the topology map or falsification attempts, and I added no other items.\n\n| Item | Rating | Why |\n|---|---|---|\n| B01 | gap | `escalate_to_human` has a `direct_route` (`config/tools.yaml:91`). When the gateway is unavailable, `src/gateway_client.py:52-59` calls the helpdesk MCP server directly. That skips the gateway's allowlist and disabled-tool checks. It is also listed as affecting B04 and E06. |\n| B02 | gap (medium confidence) | The retrieval cache key (`src/retrieval.py:42`) ignores the employee id. A model-chosen query can get another employee's cached employee-only handbook chunks, which bypasses the SQL access filter. |\n| B03 | needs_evidence | Runtime tokens last 300 seconds and the gateway checks the certificate binding. Rotation of the static DB and Anthropic secrets, and whether the downstream tokens are holder-bound, are not shown in this repo. |\n| B04 | gap | The `agent_principal` stop flag cuts off the agent without touching the employee. The direct-route fallback skips that check while tokens last 300 seconds against a 10-second stop target. `agent_type` flags are not checked at the gateway. `drop_subject` is never called. |\n| B05 | gap (medium confidence) | Every consequential tool goes through the approval gate. However, `describe()` in `src/approvals.py:31` leaves out the model-written `note` of a leave request. The approval hash covers it, so the employee approves a field they never saw. |\n\n- **Unknown checks:** B02.1, B02.3 and B02.4 depend on IAM and STS policy that live outside this repo. B03.1, B03.2 and B03.4 are unknown for the reasons in the B03 row.\n- **Out of batch:** `k8s/audit-maintenance.yaml` keeps 6 weekly audit partitions (`KEEP_PARTITIONS` 6), but the README says six months. That belongs to an audit-retention item, not this batch.\n- **Skill script flag:** `review_coverage.py` fails to import `prescan` when run with `-I`, so I ran the skill scripts without `-I`, using the same interpreter.\n- **Still empty:** I left `components`, `fix` and `assignee` empty on the gaps, since step 9 comes after challenges. `scope` is filled in."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":655,"cache_read_input_tokens":118349,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":655},"output_tokens":791,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5c0e1d7c-1c3d-4042-9555-abf3c43a76e6","uuid":"0d01c352-569c-4a5e-9ac1-cdc3929c83a5","timestamp":"2026-11-21T11:48:20.253Z","request_id":"req_011ChG29DzJx3Q6GRZzPpCQn"}
